<title>USA: Fed expected to refrain from open market action.</title>
<headline>Fed expected to refrain from open market action.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is expected to refrain from open market operations on Friday, analysts said.</p>
<p>Federal funds traded at a relatively soft 5-3/8 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target, in early dealings.</p>
<p>The Fed added $6.212 billion in temporary reserves to the banking system through four-day fixed system repurchase agreements on Thursday.</p>
<p>(( -- E. Freilich, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679))</p>
